2026-05-27 11:03:43,144 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., a consortium of specialized agents, is pleased to submit this tender proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval. Our proposed solution leverages our expertise in large language models (LLMs), retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), and cloud architecture to provide an intelligent assistance tool that integrates with existing practices and systems, ensuring efficiency, quality, and compliance with regulatory requirements.

# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks to improve the efficiency of its administrative services and the quality of service rendered to users through an artificial intelligence solution. The solution must provide assistance with information consultation, drafting, file instruction, and collaboration, while respecting regulatory constraints such as GDPR, data protection, explicability, and transparency.

# Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution is built around a SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure provider, Outscale, ensuring sovereignty and compliance with EU regulations. We will design an architecture that utilizes containerized microservices orchestrated by Kubernetes for efficient deployment, scaling, and management. For API integration, we will leverage our experience with API gateways like Kong and Apigee, and message brokers such as Apache Kafka and RabbitMQ.

To meet the requirements of assistance with information consultation, drafting, and file instruction, we propose fine-tuning our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, on a dataset specific to the City of Belval's domain. This will be complemented by a RAG-based system integrating with the client's existing information system, allowing for efficient retrieval of relevant information and recall of applicable rules.

Our solution ensures explicability and transparency through source citation, chain-of-thought display, and confidence scoring, providing recommendations that can be understood and validated by agents. We also implement strict access controls, including multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP or hardware tokens (FIDO2), role-based access control design, and privileged access management solutions like CyberArk Conjur or HashiCorp Vault.

For data protection and GDPR compliance, we will conduct a Data Protection Impact Assessment (DPIA) with an average duration of 3 weeks to identify potential risks and recommend mitigation strategies. Our solution logs all queries with SHA-256 hash chaining for immutability and integrates real-time SIEM using tools like Wazuh or Elastic SIEM for monitoring and responding to security incidents.

Our budget for this project is estimated based on a total contract value of 3 million euros over 4 years, with an annual revenue of approximately 750,000 euros. Our minimum acceptable margin percentage is 18%, which translates to a projected profit per year of around 135,000 euros and a total projected profit of approximately 540,000 euros over the duration of the contract.

To ensure sustainability and reduce energetic consumption, we have partnered with green hosting providers OVHcloud and Scaleway, both using 100% renewable energy. Our practices include INT8/INT4 model quantization reducing GPU energy by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching reducing recomputes by an estimated 20%, and a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle.

# Unaddressed Requirements
Upon reviewing the tender requirements and our agents' capabilities, we note that there are no explicitly unaddressed requirements within our proposal. However, we acknowledge the importance of continuous monitoring and adaptation to ensure full compliance and alignment with the City of Belval's evolving needs and regulatory landscapes.

# Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is confident in its ability to deliver a comprehensive artificial intelligence solution that meets the City of Belval's objectives for improving administrative efficiency and service quality while adhering to stringent regulatory and environmental standards. Our team looks forward to collaborating closely with the City of Belval to implement this project, ensuring a successful outcome that benefits both parties and contributes positively to the community and environment.
